":5},{"category":"Cajun/Creole","historical_business_count":4},{"category":"Wine Bars","historical_business_count":0}],"history":[{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Cajun/Creole, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"2QGyW4T6E_4iSltdx9i2RQ","review_id":"4e_9fewF2Qt23-Y6K4HyTA","date":"2011-09-22T20:38:27","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9472388625144958,"text_excerpt":"Pascal's Manale specializes in Creole Italian dishes but it's main focus is the BBQ shrimp (that they claim to have invented). This is my father's favorite place to go in New Orleans and I like it rather a bit myself as I have been eating here for a very long time. When you first walk in they have an awesome oyster bar (probably one of, if not the best, old school oyster bars in the city). You walk past that to find the host and you are then seated in one of two dining rooms (which used to have lots of great old photos but the building suffered extensive flooding during Katrina and all the stuff that survived is now on display in the bar area). They had a slow and painful rebuilding perio..."},{"business_id":"2QGyW4T6E_4iSltdx9i2RQ","review_id":"EYzmop8qI9vRsGi--6QOJQ","date":"2011-12-13T17:39:52","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9469279050827026,"text_excerpt":"This is a Nola institution! You simply must eat here at least once in your life. The bbq shrimp was to die for. I'll admit, I was a little frightened at first because they are served with the heads and feet on still-- but the bbq sauce they come in makes you forget that all too quickly. They're HUGE too- they make tiger prawns look like wimpy little shrimp. We started with some eggplant and crab dish. I also had a cup of the gumbo- it was soo good! What really made our experience here was our waiter. For the life of me, I cannot remember his name, but he was hilarious and gave us some great suggestions for bars and things to do. The food was great-- not the best meal we had in the city, b..."},{"business_id":"2QGyW4T6E_4iSltdx9i2RQ","review_id":"5GqkiV9-GQP6cAVC3aU3sw","date":"2011-11-18T17:18:01","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9395537376403809,"text_excerpt":"I've been to New Orleans several times and have eaten at many different restaurants from the French Quarter to the Garden District. Pascal's Manale is my very favorite restaurant to visit. I order their signature dish of barbequed shrimp every time. The waiter puts a bib around your neck and takes away your silverware. And this is a fine dining establishment, mind you! I just can't get past the shrimp to try the other dishes. Be sure to leave room for their bread pudding. I never fancied bread pudding until I tried theirs. It's decadent. :)"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"2QGyW4T6E_4iSltdx9i2RQ","photo_id":"gZzqq-N2G5EWiJfSZuplQg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/gZzqq-N2G5EWiJfSZuplQg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8804199695587158},{"business_id":"2QGyW4T6E_4iSltdx9i2RQ","photo_id":"I2BgGE8YceQdF_qEmhNsSQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/I2BgGE8YceQdF_qEmhNsSQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8737668991088867},{"business_id":"2QGyW4T6E_4iSltdx9i2RQ","photo_id":"sS1b95KXRiHVRBf7A0XSNQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/sS1b95KXRiHVRBf7A0XSNQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8712706565856934},{"business_id":"2QGyW4T6E_4iSltdx9i2RQ","photo_id":"i4VC7iegesKazmVqvPyO4g","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/i4VC7iegesKazmVqvPyO4g.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8700153827667236},{"business_id":"2QGyW4T6E_4iSltdx9i2RQ","photo_id":"yHswdtMbbYfNf5yThVnExA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/yHswdtMbbYfNf5yThVnExA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7665807008743286}]},"notebook_case":null}
